meta {
  name: 03. Connect (Query Token - Subscribe)
  type: ws
  seq: 3
}

ws {
  url: {{wsBaseUrl}}/api/v1/ws?token={{token}}
  body: ws
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:ws {
  name: ws.subscribe
  content: '''
    {
      "id": "sub-1",
      "event": "ws.subscribe",
      "channel": "{{wsChannel}}"
    }
  '''
}

docs {
  # Connect WebSocket (Query Token — Browser Style) & Subscribe

  **Protocol:** `WebSocket` (`ws://` / `wss://`)
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/ws?token=<access_token>`
  **Auth:** Query Parameter `token` (Access Token)

  ## Description
  Demonstrates the browser-compatible handshake flow where the JWT access token is passed via `?token={{token}}` (because browser `new WebSocket(url)` cannot attach custom `Authorization` headers).

  The pre-configured message subscribes this connection to `{{wsChannel}}` (default `room:test`).

  ## Expected Server Response
  ```json
  {
    "id": "sub-1",
    "event": "ws.subscribed",
    "channel": "room:test",
    "data": {
      "channel": "room:test"
    },
    "timestamp": "2026-11-26T10:30:10Z"
  }
  ```
}
